{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath","id":1483042,"title":"Did Sasha Vykos keep some spark of creativity in undeath?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-04T09:20:25-07:00","id":1483042,"title":"Did Sasha Vykos keep some spark of creativity in undeath?","content":"It's said in VTM that the children of Caine are static creatures who have lost a vital spark of creativity and adaptabilty and it gets more pronounced as they get older. It's seems that Vykos seems to put that into doubt as it's continues to adapt quite well to an everchanging world and is able to learn and master new paths of enlightment and skills. Where many of it's peers of the same age have trouble with that and sometimes withdraw and even go into topor. What is your take on this notion and do you think kindred still have that spark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T09:54:40-07:00","id":1483043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath#post1483042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's said in VTM that the children of Caine are static creatures who have lost a vital spark of creativity and adaptabilty and it gets more pronounced as they get older.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not entirely true<br /> There are several mertis that built on the fact, vampire could be indeed creative (and the True Brujah innovate too) and numerous scholar/scientist Cainite NPC made the world better (and worse. way worse) with their inventions be it magical or technological<br /> To list a few such merit:<br /> Ability Aptitude - You are particularly gifted with one Ability<br /> Common Sense - You have a significant amount of practical, everyday wisdom.<br /> Entrepreneur - Making money comes easy to the character. All difficulty of rolls that involve acquiring money through business are reduced by 2.<br /> Eye for Beauty - You are a natural critic.<br /> Magic Sensitivity - You have a supernatural gift that allows you to know if any magic is in use or has been used recently within a 10-footradius of yourself.<br /> Bardic Gift - Gifted by the Muses, you sing sweetly, play an instrument divinely and speak with passion and eloquence.<br /> Well-Traveled - The character has traveled all over the globe, seen many different cities, and met a great number of Kindred<br /> Refined - You are a member of the elite. You are at home in high society and you never feel out of place around the 'beautiful people'.<br /> Gifted - The difficulties of all Craft and Expression rolls are reduced by three<br /> Greater Colors - The vampire sees colors more distinctly and with greater definition. The world is far more colorful. Unfortunately, the vampire is more likely to become enraptured by colorful objects.<br /> Oracular Ability - You see signs and omens in everyday life.<br /> University - The character has control over a university. The trustees and important officials serve his interests. The character has full access to the school, and he can hunt the campus freely. The professors and libraries are useful in providing him with research information. The campus also has lots of computer equipment, along with those who know how to use it.<br /> Capable Assistant - The character has another vampire who acts as her right hand in everything. This vampire is loyal, capable, and powerful enough to stand against anyone in her way. She may be Blood Bound to the character but would serve anyway<br /> Just to name a few, not to ention the Backgrounds....<br /> Anyhow!<br /> Uriel then cursed Caine and his childer to cling to Darkness, drink only blood, eat only ashes, and be frozen at the point of death, cursed so all they touch would crumble into nothing.<br /> Obviously, the &quot;eat only ashes&quot; part never really realised, they are undead and drink blood, but the &quot;all they touch would crumble into nothing&quot; thing more or less true and a bit of what you described, but in a different angle<br /> Vampire ara able to adapt (more then one Path actually require this adatpability) and create<br /> The catch: no matter how creative they are, no matter how well they adapt, no matter what they do, hey are essentially doomed to fail. Either by fate or by the hands of others (Second City, Carthage, the Dream, the Hunedoara Castle-inconnu school; most of the Cainite projects crumbled, it was just a matter of time)<br /> And Caine added his own curse to the mix, so after the 2nd and 3rd, each generation will be weaker and jelous to the power and blood of their &quot;betters&quot; and would seek to rebel, like they did, to destroy them if not kept in short leash","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T09:56:35-07:00","id":1483044,"title":"","content":"Yes, they still have that &quot;spark.&quot; Or, rather, they're not inherently without it.<br /> <br /> My take on the &quot;stasis&quot; of vampires is that it's psychological. The loss of creativity is ennui and depression. You live forever surrounded by assholes in a shitty world that doesn't get better as most of the world you knew dies. There is nothing new under the sun, and you'll struggle to connect to future eras because the Masquerade makes long lasting, direct personal connections difficult. Whatever you create you will inevitably watch succumb to entropy and disappear from the world. It's pointless. You get bored, you get lonely, you stop caring and you stop trying or paying attention.<br /> <br /> If you can maintain the drive to keep going, have something to care about such as a greater purpose, you're less likely to succumb<br /> <br /> Crankiness at one's changing surroundings is also part of human thought. I'm still irrationally offended by a lot of the changes in my city that have occurred since I was a child. My grandparents feel that even stronger. It's like watching parts of your life being erased, in a way, to make room for somebody elses world - especially if it's replaced with something you don't particularly care for. Elders and Methuselahs may have lost entire cultures, nationalities and languages to progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-04-2022, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:05:17-07:00","id":1483070,"title":"","content":"I like to think mostly, vampires, especially older ones, mostly lose their 'spark' little by little. I think it would have something to do with the fall of Humanity (or whatever morality and sensibility it has) in most cases, besides de ennui, jading and etc.. <br /> <br /> But, I think something that would allow vamps to surpass this block, this deafening of their bright creativity, would be the blood of humans. The emotions, the humors and resonances, the memories, it would all mingle with the Kindred's and its other victims. I like to treat vampires thematically as copycats, maintainers, alien tinkerers and stealers; even their most inspired creation would be (maybe only in metaknowledge) because of the blood they drink, and the Life and Emotion they absorb through it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think Vykos could be very much a creative fella, drinking blood without reservations as an inhuman thing they &quot;is&quot;. That is a way I think justifies how Toreador can (but not always) keep inspiration, because they take care and invest in their herd and vessels, and Tzimisce are all about refining and producing the best Herd. Brujah just seem attracted to the emotional and livid mortals. While Ventrue would be that boring archetype because they mostly drink with much restriction, without interest in making a grand and fantastic drinking vessel, just a clean, quality and guaranteed feeding herd.<br /> <br /> That is how I like to think anyhow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:48:29-07:00","id":1483076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483044#post1483044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they still have that &quot;spark.&quot; Or, rather, they're not inherently without it.<br /> <br /> My take on the &quot;stasis&quot; of vampires is that it's psychological. The loss of creativity is ennui and depression. You live forever surrounded by assholes in a shitty world that doesn't get better as most of the world you knew dies. There is nothing new under the sun, and you'll struggle to connect to future eras because the Masquerade makes long lasting, direct personal connections difficult. Whatever you create you will inevitably watch succumb to entropy and disappear from the world. It's pointless. You get bored, you get lonely, you stop caring and you stop trying or paying attention.<br /> <br /> If you can maintain the drive to keep going, have something to care about such as a greater purpose, you're less likely to succumb<br /> <br /> Crankiness at one's changing surroundings is also part of human thought. I'm still irrationally offended by a lot of the changes in my city that have occurred since I was a child. My grandparents feel that even stronger. It's like watching parts of your life being erased, in a way, to make room for somebody elses world - especially if it's replaced with something you don't particularly care for. Elders and Methuselahs may have lost entire cultures, nationalities and languages to progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that better than the idea that becoming a vampire just inherently robs the person of creativity. Part of the curse of being a vampire isn't a mystical curse at all. It's just the side effect of living for centuries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:55:37-07:00","id":1483078,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles, I hold that 1) vampires are inherently parasitic creatures and 2) that only the living can truly possess the creative inspiration to create something &quot;new&quot;. Vampires can be very intelligent, technically proficient, and learn new things, but like Morgoth and Sauron they can only imitate or corrupt, not innovate or really create. They could create very attractive and pleasing work of arts that surpass much of the product of ordinary human artists, but they will just never match the &quot;wow&quot; factor of Van Gogh, Picasso, Bouguereau, the Renaissance greats, and so on (in whatever field).<br /> <br /> High humanity vampires (say 8+) might be able to sometimes approximate that lost spark, but it's rare.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I believe becoming a vampire is an awful thing. Despite the cool powers and other seductive elements of the undead, it's not a good thing and always comes at too high a price. If that isn't the case, I believe the genre is being done wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T21:47:30-07:00","id":1483103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483078#post1483078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I believe becoming a vampire is an awful thing. Despite the cool powers and other seductive elements of the undead, it's not a good thing and always comes at too high a price. If that isn't the case, I believe the genre is being done wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have loved 1st Edition Requiem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think having to give up your family (or risk them being declared a Masquerade breach), never being able to go out during the day, and having the Beast inside of you for your eternity is more than enough of a price. Not to mention the (literally) cutthroat politics of the Vampire world (in both settings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-05-2022, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T21:47:30-07:00","id":1483104,"title":"","content":"Sorry, double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":".  Double post. 06-05-2022, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T05:05:57-07:00","id":1483211,"title":"","content":"I had a theory that vampiric creativity is stunted by discipline development. By routing all their will into the development of their powers they neglect their inherent ability to learn and grow. Combined with a sedentary routine based life and vampires creativity is stiffled.<br /> <br /> Vykos by contrast has a very interesting life and a series of passions and project so it'd make sense its more creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-06-2022, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T18:14:11-07:00","id":1483428,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that the setting distinguishes <b>creativity</b> and <b>adaptability</b>\u200b. The core books lore conforms to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s interpretation, but it also states that vampires are exceptionally good at adapting to blend with the prey, things like getting new accents and learning new technologies comes as second nature. As anyone can notice, of course, it isn't completely consistent not even in the same book. But it is still there. <br /> <br /> By myself, while anguishing over lost creativity is fun, sometimes interpreting what it means is more confusing than useful and staying true to it end up harming the game, either because some player want to explore some creative outlet with the character, or because it stays in the way for making an interesting NPC. It even stays true for some vampire stories you may want to tell elsewhere.<br /> <br /> For this reason I not only disagree that letting vampires be creative is doing the genre wrong, I hold that being too strict with it may be worse for your game.<br /> <br /> Not to say that, in the end, telling a vampire story is a creative exercise. How can you be sure that you're properly conveying lack of creativity through your character when the character itself is a creative outlet?<br /> <br /> How do you even define creativity to do that? I can guarantee that by most technical definitions of creativity the notion of &quot;losing the spark&quot; is nonsense, as that would mean a loss of the ability to develop solutions to presented problems instead of only recurring to set solutions, which isn't something I've ever saw any vampire being bound to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T20:01:21-07:00","id":1483437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483428#post1483428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to consider is that the setting distinguishes <b>creativity</b> and <b>adaptability</b>\u200b. The core books lore conforms to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s interpretation, but it also states that vampires are exceptionally good at adapting to blend with the prey, things like getting new accents and learning new technologies comes as second nature. As anyone can notice, of course, it isn't completely consistent not even in the same book. But it is still there.<br /> <br /> By myself, while anguishing over lost creativity is fun, sometimes interpreting what it means is more confusing than useful and staying true to it end up harming the game, either because some player want to explore some creative outlet with the character, or because it stays in the way for making an interesting NPC. It even stays true for some vampire stories you may want to tell elsewhere.<br /> <br /> For this reason I not only disagree that letting vampires be creative is doing the genre wrong, I hold that being too strict with it may be worse for your game.<br /> <br /> Not to say that, in the end, telling a vampire story is a creative exercise. How can you be sure that you're properly conveying lack of creativity through your character when the character itself is a creative outlet?<br /> <br /> How do you even define creativity to do that? I can guarantee that by most technical definitions of creativity the notion of &quot;losing the spark&quot; is nonsense, as that would mean a loss of the ability to develop solutions to presented problems instead of only recurring to set solutions, which isn't something I've ever saw any vampire being bound to.</div> </div> </div> </div>^this<br /> Creativity is so intrinsic to intelligence that it is difficult to imagine what an intelligence over 2 would even represent without creativity. Is the vampire, what, really good at math?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T09:31:52-07:00","id":1483472,"title":"","content":"To me, there's creativity and then there's creativity. You can creatively experiment and combine known elements and impressions to something that's more impressive than the sum of its parts, and you can pour something out that's unmistakable and uniquely <b>you</b> and <b>yours</b>. Kindred should be able to accomplish the former or they'd just never be able to function, and Toreadors wouldn't have any authority as artists whatsoever, while being doomed to feel like hacks and fakers for never managing the latter after their dying day.<br /> <br /> Am currently playing a Toreador musician who's spent his unlife composing masterful - but never groundbreaking - songs while completely failing to finish what would have been his magnum opus, who has rationalized the Embrace and teaching of his Childe as his one and only true act of creation since his death to balance out his bitterness and grief at the loss of his own potential.<br /> <br /> A vampire can paint a gorgeous painting or write a cool movie, but no-one is ever going to see or watch it and wonder where in the world the ideas came from. You're doomed to, at best, be on the banal side of brilliant. Which is the sort of fate that would drive most true artists to near-suicide.<br /> <br /> It just so happens that Vykos doesn't have a whole lot of critics to point out that all her experiments are a little bit obvious given the means, motivation and the time to think of them she's had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","user":"Mr Sharp","date":". 06-09-2022, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","name":"Mr Sharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T09:57:52-07:00","id":1483476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483437#post1483437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creativity is so intrinsic to intelligence that it is difficult to imagine what an intelligence over 2 would even represent without creativity. Is the vampire, what, really good at math?</div> </div> </div> </div>For most current scientific theories on intelligence it is impossible, without creativity you would have an Intelligence Score of 0. How well you perform a task is meaningless if you're unable to even slightly adapt anything to other tasks. An entity without creativity under such theories can only solve a problem it already knows the solution, or at least has a strict procedure to solve.<br /> <br /> Yes, it could be really good at math. Like a regular computer not running a neural network, because even the simplest neural network today has a primitive creative process.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a formal view following technical definitions. It applies, because this <b>is</b> also about the kind of phenomena we usually call creativity, but it doesn't have to bear a weight on fiction necessarily. I just think it is too awkward to enforce this view of lack of creativity as necessary, simple or logical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Sharp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483472#post1483472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, there's creativity and then there's creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, but everything I posted before still applies.<br /> <br /> As I said, playing the anguish of the loss of this spark may be lots of fun. I've did that too many times and still do from time to time. But when not in the mood to, or when a player wants to be a creative vampire, I just let it be.<br /> <br /> From a scientific standpoint, as far as it matters, being able to imprint yourself in your work is even more basic. You don't need to be an artistic genius, or even barely good, to do that, you just naturally do, because that's a result of everything you know being filtered by the unique features of your body, your perception, your understanding and your memories. To not be able to do that you would have to be a mass-produced machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:33:34-07:00","id":1483483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483476#post1483476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you mean, but everything I posted before still applies.<br /> <br /> As I said, playing the anguish of the loss of this spark may be lots of fun. I've did that too many times and still do from time to time. But when not in the mood to, or when a player wants to be a creative vampire, I just let it be.<br /> <br /> From a scientific standpoint, as far as it matters, being able to imprint yourself in your work is even more basic. You don't need to be an artistic genius, or even barely good, to do that, you just naturally do, because that's a result of everything you know being filtered by the unique features of your body, your perception, your understanding and your memories. To not be able to do that you would have to be a mass-produced machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't responding to you at all. Also didn't say you needed to be an artistic genius to implement the depth of your own essential experience as a human being in your work - though I'm fairly certain it IS both harder and rarer than it sounds like you give it credit for, definitely not something basic that everyone is capable of just because you and the people you tend to associate with are - just that that's the element of creativity where I find it makes the most sense for vampires to inherently fall short.<br /> <br /> I've had a load of fun making plenty of creative vampires too, but if I was the Storyteller and one of the players wanted to play 'the absolute rising star of modern fashion, revolutionizing the industry with her own amazing and unique vision for the future that shocks people right to the core and inspires everyone&quot; then I'd tell them that sorry, that's a level of connection to the rest of humanity that Kindred just don't have anymore, and to rework their concept to something a bit more grounded that better fits the tone of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","name":"Mr Sharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T11:09:19-07:00","id":1483493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Sharp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483483#post1483483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't responding to you at all. Also didn't say you needed to be an artistic genius to implement the depth of your own essential experience as a human being in your work - though I'm fairly certain it IS both harder and rarer than it sounds like you give it credit for, definitely not something basic that everyone is capable of just because you and the people you tend to associate with are - just that that's the element of creativity where I find it makes the most sense for vampires to inherently fall short.<br /> <br /> I've had a load of fun making plenty of creative vampires too, but if I was the Storyteller and one of the players wanted to play 'the absolute rising star of modern fashion, revolutionizing the industry with her own amazing and unique vision for the future that shocks people right to the core and inspires everyone&quot; then I'd tell them that sorry, that's a level of connection to the rest of humanity that Kindred just don't have anymore, and to rework their concept to something a bit more grounded that better fits the tone of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't assumed you were responding to me, I just cited my previous post for ease of reference.<br /> <br /> Other than that I'd like you don't try to draw conclusions about me based on your disagreement with what I said. I'm not an artist talking about my personal experience, I'm a psychologist talking in the broadest terms about the body of research and academic debate on the matters at discussion.<br /> <br /> You imprint something of yourself in everything you do. So much so that we have whole bodies of research on identification through the imprint of the author in all sorts of creations and that's just one aspect of it, and none of those require the author to have any particular level of skill or creativity.<br /> <br /> As I said, it is just a side note as far as it goes than something that by itself should inform your game. It just means that from a technical standpoint it is impossible to truly define a character as non-creative. As for your standing on what to do if a player wants to play a character with amazingly inspiring levels of creativity, I get what you mean and possibly would follow a similar route if I think it will disrupt the game, which it has a high probability of doing anyway, but I wouldn't be so closed to the option if it is really important to the player and the actual concept in the actual circumstance seems interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T13:02:22-07:00","id":1483505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483493#post1483493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't assumed you were responding to me, I just cited my previous post for ease of reference.<br /> <br /> Other than that I'd like you don't try to draw conclusions about me based on your disagreement with what I said. I'm not an artist talking about my personal experience, I'm a psychologist talking in the broadest terms about the body of research and academic debate on the matters at discussion.<br /> <br /> You imprint something of yourself in everything you do. So much so that we have whole bodies of research on identification through the imprint of the author in all sorts of creations and that's just one aspect of it, and none of those require the author to have any particular level of skill or creativity.<br /> <br /> As I said, it is just a side note as far as it goes than something that by itself should inform your game. It just means that from a technical standpoint it is impossible to truly define a character as non-creative. As for your standing on what to do if a player wants to play a character with amazingly inspiring levels of creativity, I get what you mean and possibly would follow a similar route if I think it will disrupt the game, which it has a high probability of doing anyway, but I wouldn't be so closed to the option if it is really important to the player and the actual concept in the actual circumstance seems interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a psychologist, then, would you or would you not say that I'm obligated to respect the picture you liberally and intimately paint of me and everyone else in the world that I very specifically don't recognize from myself or the varied people I've known in-depth in my life, the authority of which is based on the musings of consummate intellectuals most likely from another continent whom I have no reason to expect to have anything in common with, which opinion I most critically<i> did not solicit </i>before you suddenly decided it was something I needed in my life?<br /> <br /> And if you perchance found that I was not, in fact, obligated to respect that view, would you say that you trying to push it on me out of nowhere would be a bigger or smaller assumption on your part than me assuming you were just talking from your own experience alone and those of the people around you was on mine? No comment on the assuming you were an artist thing. I didn't.<br /> <br /> This wasn't the response I was originally gonna to write, but I guess I'm going to try to be Socratic instead of getting mired in another one of these recursive autistic back-and-forths where we keep putting words in each others' mouths and passive-aggressively correcting the other ad infinitum because we're not actually talking about the same thing, let alone coming at it with the same intentions. Consider yourself lucky. I'm very good at those, or at least very persistent, and you might be the first I've ever spared.<br /> <br /> And yeah, still no for my part. The tone of the game affects everyone at the table, and that player being very attached to their inspirational fashionesta wouldn't trump that for me. I'm sure I could help them come up with ways to flesh the concept out into something more manageable and realistic they could get excited about too if they couldn't by themselves, but if they refused to budge then it'd be straight back to the drawing board. Think I'd have very little tolerance for players who only care about their own ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","name":"Mr Sharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:00:15-07:00","id":1483524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Sharp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1483505#post1483505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a psychologist, then, would you or would you not say that I'm obligated to respect the picture you liberally and intimately paint of me and everyone else in the world that I very specifically don't recognize from myself or the varied people I've known in-depth in my life, the authority of which is based on the musings of consummate intellectuals most likely from another continent whom I have no reason to expect to have anything in common with, which opinion I most critically<i> did not solicit </i>before you suddenly decided it was something I needed in my life?<br /> <br /> And if you perchance found that I was not, in fact, obligated to respect that view, would you say that you trying to push it on me out of nowhere would be a bigger or smaller assumption on your part than me assuming you were just talking from your own experience alone and those of the people around you was on mine? No comment on the assuming you were an artist thing. I didn't.<br /> <br /> This wasn't the response I was originally gonna to write, but I guess I'm going to try to be Socratic instead of getting mired in another one of these recursive autistic back-and-forths where we keep putting words in each others' mouths and passive-aggressively correcting the other ad infinitum because we're not actually talking about the same thing, let alone coming at it with the same intentions. Consider yourself lucky. I'm very good at those, or at least very persistent, and you might be the first I've ever spared.<br /> <br /> And yeah, still no for my part. The tone of the game affects everyone at the table, and that player being very attached to their inspirational fashionesta wouldn't trump that for me. I'm sure I could help them come up with ways to flesh the concept out into something more manageable and realistic they could get excited about too if they couldn't by themselves, but if they refused to budge then it'd be straight back to the drawing board. Think I'd have very little tolerance for players who only care about their own ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please don't use autistic as an insult, I speak as a neuroatypical person<br /> <br /> Also, this conversation line has gotten argumentative and way off topic.<br /> <br /> Please move on.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T10:25:08-07:00","id":1483721,"title":"","content":"I didn't expect my post would get so many responses and for the most part you gave interesting answers and I forgot the merits and flaws of the earlier editions that help with the kindred to stave off boredom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T07:10:19-07:00","id":1484108,"title":"","content":"IMO, Vampire is chock-full of melodramatic unreliable narrators. <br /> <br /> Clearly BS:<br /> Vampires are static and unchanging (they can raise attributes like intelligence and drive them over the limits of humans, I doubt that) <br /> Vampire politics is nightmarish (like you've got centuries ahead of you, you need to manage your own domains. Is it likely that you'll have elysium every week and always mess with one another? Not really. You have humans and ghouls to abuse, you don't really need to screw with neonates that much) <br /> Elders are always assholes. <br /> It's the Camarilla's fault<br /> The Anarchs can be big and viable. <br /> Methuselahs thirst<br /> Vampire books after... Yeah, I can't say that. <br /> <br /> The Text actually agrees with me in parts~<br /> -The Sabbat are Evil-stupid: they don't do monstrous shit all the time in their own territories. <br /> <br /> I have my reservations:<br /> Vampires don't do sex well. (like, I realize there's in-game mechanical difficulties and some fairly good story/biological reasons, but do you know how much easier the masquerade would be if this were false? A lot, so I'm ignoring it.)<br /> <br /> BS I like: <br /> Gehenna. Always around the corner. Really, there's a very good chance the ancients will just continue business as usual when they wake up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T13:54:48-07:00","id":1484135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483042-did-sasha-vykos-keep-some-spark-of-creativity-in-undeath?p=1484108#post1484108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BS I like:<br /> Gehenna. Always around the corner. Really, there's a very good chance the ancients will just continue business as usual when they wake up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a very good chance most of them are already awake in the 90's yet the world is just business as usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join D